WEBVTT

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.460
My name is Minashiro Soushi.

00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:08.010
By the time you listen to this,

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:10.650
I will no longer be in this world.

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:31.030
The 22nd century turned into a
period of war for all humanity.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:39.880
Unknown beings that arrived from
distant space, the Festum...

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.800
Forty years after they arrived on this planet,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.230
possessing power beyond human understanding,

00:01:05.270 --> 00:01:08.330
most of the world became a battlefield.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.490
Entering combat area.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.140
Sixty seconds to landing!

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:20.140
All men, assume mission formation.

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:22.770
Upon landing, join the front line
immediately, as per the plan.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:24.180
Ready?

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:24.770
Yes, sir!

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:32.270
You are the elite who made it through
rigorous training to survive this long.

00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:33.780
I consider it an honor

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:36.780
to fight with you.

00:01:42.700 --> 00:01:43.700
Commence operation!

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:49.000
First machine, departing!

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.050
Second machine, on the way!

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.310
This is worse than the reports said.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:16.000
Second machine, Olympia Angels, landing check.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:16.780
Bro...

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.280
I'll fight, too, just like you.

00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.370
Go, Billy.

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:25.810
Fourth machine, moving out!

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:32.790
Fifth machine, heading out!

00:02:36.010 --> 00:02:37.260
Sixth machine, moving out!

00:02:40.150 --> 00:02:44.600
Thought-controlled, man-piloted battle
mechas designed to fight the Festum,

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.520
the Fafners.

00:02:47.610 --> 00:02:49.480
Only the chosen can pilot them.

00:02:49.970 --> 00:02:51.290
They are the ace up our sleeve.

00:02:52.050 --> 00:02:54.190
Types 1, 2, and 3 sighted.

00:02:54.190 --> 00:02:55.760
Watch for Type 4.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:00.100
They are equipped with enemy components,

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:02.950
making their power work for humanity.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:11.050
Without the Fafners, we would
have been eliminated long ago.

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:17.130
Even if victory remains far out of reach,

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.380
we were able to buy enough time to foster hope.

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:30.050
Mauna Kea Patrol Base has fallen.

00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:32.060
The enemy has taken over all functions!

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:34.510
Hurry up with the evacuation.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:36.570
Gather all forces at the northern end!

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.860
Defense Unit 1 has been annihilated!

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.570
Two kilometers before they reach
Big Island's last defensive line!

00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:43.970
Get out of there, General Narain!

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:47.550
Quiet! This is the largest transport
base in the Pacific region.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:51.420
If this base falls, millions will starve to death.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.580
Defend it at any cost!

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:56.980
They never even looked at this place before.

00:03:57.450 --> 00:04:02.680
Has the Festum learned the way
humans preserve their lives?

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:13.940
We still can't get on?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.880
But they're right on top of us!

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.860
Calm down. You can board soon.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:20.450
Mauna Kea will be okay, right?

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.090
I'm sure we'll win.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.960
Are we going to die?

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.530
What is that?

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.450
HQ has declared ROE Alpha.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:08.120
Target: the entirety of Big Island!

00:05:09.270 --> 00:05:11.130
What?

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:13.400
HQ's aerial strike force is approaching.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.460
No...

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:16.330
Connect to the Neo United Nations HQ!

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:18.790
Give the order in my name to halt the attack!

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:23.460
We have troops out there fighting!

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.470
Not to mention thousands of citizens!

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:28.470
ROE Alpha is absolute.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.640
Retract the order!

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.420
Fool.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.460
Major Walter, you are divested of your authority.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.140
Apprehend him.

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:42.150
General Narain has given the
order to halt the attack.

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:43.220
Too late.

00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:45.400
Input point. Attack formation.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.530
Stop!

00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:23.440
Don't, General!

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.780
Everyone, look for survivors!

00:06:26.520 --> 00:06:32.130
I shot an ally... I...

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:37.290
It's hopeless... Hey, is anyone alive?

00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:50.550
It's no use... We can't win.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:03.570
Why did we fight?

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:06.070
What was it for?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:12.710
As the world was exhausted by long years of war,

00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:18.730
the faint hope—that if both sides
could understand each other,

00:07:19.860 --> 00:07:22.980
then perhaps the war would end—

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:27.000
began to make its way into
some corner of our world.

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:11.630
Tatsumiyajima...

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:14.860
A man-made island, built after
Japan was destroyed in the war,

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:19.700
in hopes of leaving behind a peaceful civilization.

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:22.430
This is where I once lived.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.610
The regionals aren't far off!

00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:03.680
Keep your spirits up!

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.770
Mimika hears ya, Coach Kaname!

00:09:07.590 --> 00:09:10.360
Mikamika, you don't take this seriously!

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:16.910
Kondou-sensei?

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.740
Oh, it's you, Sakura... Is someone hurt?

00:09:20.740 --> 00:09:22.460
Let them rest a bit.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:25.090
Excuse me...

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:27.050
Please take them!

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:30.610
Back to it! Oh...

00:09:31.210 --> 00:09:32.800
Sorry to intrude!

00:09:33.570 --> 00:09:34.720
Thanks...

00:09:38.000 --> 00:09:41.720
Looking at her makes me
think of the old Kazuki.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:44.190
The "old" Kazuki, yes.

00:09:45.100 --> 00:09:48.480
Hey! Want to grab dinner at Kazuki's place today?

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:51.440
Oh, so you don't like my cooking?

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:53.280
Th-That's not what I meant.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:57.450
Love—

00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.700
Gobain!

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:04.250
Douma Hiroto Special: Pursuing the
Mysterious, Giant Creature.

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:06.630
How many TV shows is that idiot Hiroto making?
Good morning, Tatsumiyajima!

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:07.210
Today, we're pursuing Tatsumiyajima's—

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:09.860
And Seri goes along with it too much.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.340
Man, I'm bored, and it's hot.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:15.460
Grandma, I wanna work for Alvis!

00:10:18.560 --> 00:10:21.520
Don't dedicate all your studying to the art of war.

00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:24.470
You need to carry on this island's culture, as well.

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:26.780
H-Hello, Rina-senp—

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:31.810
What do you want, Kaburagi?

00:10:32.450 --> 00:10:34.150
U-Um...

00:10:34.630 --> 00:10:35.820
I'll take this!

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:38.450
Didn't you buy this yesterday?

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.740
Huh? Um, that one's for storage...

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:42.450
And this, too!

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:45.890
Kaburagi, you're the student
council president, you know.

00:10:45.890 --> 00:10:47.140
If you're buying all this manga,

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.370
do you have everything ready
for the Tanabata Festival?

00:10:49.370 --> 00:10:53.090
W-Well, without you there, all the
work keeps getting delayed...

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:55.210
You're pathetic.

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.200
Why don't we have the next meeting
together at Kazuki-senpai's place?

00:10:58.200 --> 00:11:00.590
S-Sure! That'd be great!

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:06.600
Um, Rina-senpai... Are you free later?

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:09.470
Huh? I'm working here.

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:11.010
Of course I'm not free.

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:12.680
I guess not...

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:18.110
Dense.

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:43.730
Mark Sechs Mod, arm-drive system installed.

00:11:43.730 --> 00:11:45.600
Proceed with FTP test.

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:47.700
Connection confirmed.

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:50.100
You've come a long way, Canon.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:52.400
Because you taught me, Mom...

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.410
We're crew and instructor here.

00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:56.860
Yes, Hazama-sensei!

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:00.880
Now, let's go and get something to eat.

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.660
If you stay in there all day, you'll get sick.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:04.640
Roger.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.780
Would you prefer Kazuki-kun's place again?

00:12:08.750 --> 00:12:11.330
I don't really care where...

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.040
Okay, come on out.

00:12:14.730 --> 00:12:15.380
Roger.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.330
I didn't want anyone to pilot it again...

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:26.470
We really have to rebuild it?

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:33.480
I'm surprised Canon is training to be an engineer.

00:12:33.820 --> 00:12:35.880
For someone so young, she's amazing.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:37.940
She says she wants to learn from you, too.

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:41.320
I think I'll retire. I have to finish this, anyway.

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.820
Is this really going to be educational material?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.200
Hard to say.

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.970
I couldn't turn down a request from Nishio-sensei.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:49.930
Yeah...

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.500
I think it's time to get something to eat.

00:12:53.500 --> 00:12:54.500
You're right.

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:56.910
Up we go...

00:12:56.910 --> 00:12:59.100
The usual curry it is, then.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.000
Agreed.

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:09.020
It's still not done? We won't be ready for lunch.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:10.680
Don't worry! Leave it to me!

00:13:11.010 --> 00:13:12.180
It's Mikado!

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:13.930
I'll carry it to the back.

00:13:14.530 --> 00:13:15.620
Thanks for always bringing them.

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:16.450
Not at all.

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.440
Did you make those?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.690
Yes, my dad taught me.

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:26.740
Amazing.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:29.420
Anyway, Kazuki-san, you have a customer.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.960
Soushi... You're early.

00:13:31.960 --> 00:13:34.070
Yeah, I finished my morning research.

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.330
Looks like you're still getting
ready, so I'll come later.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.380
Come on in. You'll have the staff meal, right?

00:13:40.860 --> 00:13:42.650
Yeah. Thanks.

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:48.340
Thank you for waiting.

00:13:48.910 --> 00:13:50.440
It's Akira curry.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:52.590
Oh, is this a new item?

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:56.350
No, but naming it after the one who
made it is the rule here, right?

00:13:56.580 --> 00:13:57.880
Like "Kazuki curry."

00:13:58.430 --> 00:14:01.110
Mizoguchi-san gave it that name, not me.

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:05.860
I respect you, Kazuki-senpai,
but I won't lose to you.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:07.510
Yeah, yeah.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:11.870
Where are Toumi and Mizoguchi-san?

00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:15.870
In the air. Lately, they're always flying.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:20.220
I thought I'd get to work with Toumi-senpai...

00:14:32.540 --> 00:14:34.390
Arrows to control.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:37.390
Unknown, follow. Input seeker.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.980
Not bad, little girl. Then how about this?

00:14:46.200 --> 00:14:47.490
Target: Fox One!

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:53.510
Grace to Arrows. You ran out.

00:14:54.290 --> 00:14:58.500
You can't overtake your enemy
just because you can fly faster.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.750
Man!

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:09.670
Wow, you're riding in a big airplane?
Aren't you scared?

00:15:10.500 --> 00:15:12.390
Wow! Really?

00:15:12.390 --> 00:15:18.810
That Miwa... Recently, she's always
talking to her imaginary friend.

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:22.600
Maybe it's because there aren't
any other kids her age around.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.580
I don't think it's anything to worry about.

00:15:25.580 --> 00:15:30.270
She's a very sensitive girl, so I can't help worrying.

00:15:31.460 --> 00:15:35.580
Yeah, Maya-oneechan is
flying in an airplane, too.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.720
It won't be long now, Emery.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.790
For Canon, a melon float and...

00:15:54.640 --> 00:15:55.170
Here.

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:58.860
Wh-What's this? I didn't order them.

00:15:58.860 --> 00:15:59.720
On the house.

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:01.770
Because you come here so often.

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:03.480
You like those, right?

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:07.230
I don't dislike them...

00:16:12.990 --> 00:16:16.470
Toumi's in aviation, Canon's in engineering,

00:16:16.470 --> 00:16:19.180
Kenji's in medicine, and Kaname's in education.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:21.720
Everyone's decided on their paths.

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:25.070
And you're going into research?
That seems suited to you.

00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:27.730
What about you? Cooking at a coffee shop?

00:16:29.190 --> 00:16:30.340
I'm surprisingly good at it.

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:34.670
If you wanted to use your valuable
experience as a former ace pilot,

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.340
you could be an instructor.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.910
Even after leaving the Fafner, it hasn't gone away.

00:16:42.400 --> 00:16:46.400
It's a small-scale assimilation phenomenon
resulting from the Nibelung connection.

00:16:47.030 --> 00:16:48.900
Someday, I'll find a way to cure you.

00:16:49.970 --> 00:16:52.580
I don't want to learn something
new and start working on it,

00:16:53.090 --> 00:16:57.080
only to end up leaving it unfinished.

00:16:57.870 --> 00:17:00.010
Don't you feel that way, Soushi?

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.800
There's always the possibility of recovery.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:03.910
Don't be pessimistic.

00:17:04.150 --> 00:17:06.630
I'm not. Three more years...

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:10.150
If I have that long, I can resolve myself.

00:17:11.650 --> 00:17:13.920
I can even see now.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:19.220
This place is peaceful,

00:17:20.190 --> 00:17:21.970
and it's where my closest friends were.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.430
I'll stay here.

00:17:58.470 --> 00:18:00.440
Hello, Tsubaki-chan.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:06.480
Thank you for always protecting the island.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.410
What is it? What's wrong, Tsubaki-chan?

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:24.260
Is she reacting to something?

00:18:26.260 --> 00:18:28.620
CDC. Unknown approaching!

00:18:29.050 --> 00:18:31.810
Shield line achieved in ninety seconds.

00:18:31.810 --> 00:18:33.490
Target engage!

00:18:33.490 --> 00:18:37.170
Target merge. Reference C300 Super Galaxy.

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:39.110
It's a large Human Army transport craft.

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:40.640
Human Army?

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.440
Can you sense them?

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:53.450
Yes.

00:18:55.780 --> 00:18:58.490
She's on a very pretty island.

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:06.910
Emery...

00:19:07.190 --> 00:19:07.910
General!

00:19:08.760 --> 00:19:09.320
Yes.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:12.420
Emery sensed her, too.

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.590
You don't want us to meet?

00:19:26.360 --> 00:19:29.570
Grace to CDC. Emergency.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.190
Arrows, follow, engage!

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:31.960
Roger.

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:38.990
I'm going out, Grandma!

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.400
Status?

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:46.690
Report from Kestrel in practice maneuvers.

00:19:46.690 --> 00:19:48.760
Human Army transport craft approaching.

00:19:48.760 --> 00:19:50.000
State of emergency.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.710
Worm of unknown mass detected
outside shield range.

00:19:53.710 --> 00:19:55.470
No response from Solomon.

00:19:55.880 --> 00:19:57.750
All burgs to intercept formation.

00:19:57.750 --> 00:20:00.010
Welle Shields 1 and 2 deployed.

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:03.220
Maintain course. Fafners, stand by.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:05.990
Don't strike. They haven't discovered the island.

00:20:06.980 --> 00:20:09.890
The Human Army is only being chased...

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.390
Should we ignore it?

00:20:13.720 --> 00:20:16.250
Communication request from residential area.
The Hino household.

00:20:16.250 --> 00:20:16.900
Put them through.

00:20:17.180 --> 00:20:17.970
I'm sorry. Yes, Miwa-chan suddenly...

00:20:17.970 --> 00:20:20.040
Please, Mama! Please!

00:20:20.040 --> 00:20:21.680
It's all right, Miwa. Calm down.
I'm sorry. Yes, Miwa-chan suddenly...

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:22.610
Yes, she's saying, "Help the airplane."

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.710
She's calling for help right now.

00:20:24.710 --> 00:20:25.930
Yes, she's saying, "Help the airplane."

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:33.460
Man, Gobain is so awesome!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:37.270
Sui, didn't you buy the same magazine yesterday?

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:38.480
Huh? Did I?

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:40.230
Request for Offensive Action

00:20:40.720 --> 00:20:41.350
Waffe Laden is now on standby.

00:20:41.350 --> 00:20:43.470
It changed to a request for offensive action!

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:45.160
So it is an enemy!

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:48.220
The lighting in this clip could be better...

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:50.430
Don't make so many of them!

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.770
I'm not going along with you anymore.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:54.420
This time, it's a real fight.

00:20:54.420 --> 00:20:57.000
You think we'll get to pilot Fafners?

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:59.690
Without a connection test?
Nah, we'll be watching.

00:20:59.690 --> 00:21:04.450
That's right! I haven't made a
helmet like Hiroto-senpai yet!

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:05.980
You don't need one.

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.450
Arriving momentarily.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:08.560
Here.

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:12.380
My senpai handed it down to me.

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:13.960
Take good care of it.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:15.700
Hiroto-senpai...

00:21:16.960 --> 00:21:18.550
Thank you!

00:21:18.550 --> 00:21:19.960
Arrival.

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:22.960
He's so cool!

00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:31.430
You sure it was okay to give
her your good luck charm?

00:21:32.180 --> 00:21:34.970
I can only pilot a Fafner for a few more years.

00:21:34.970 --> 00:21:37.730
I've gotta hand it down while I can!

00:21:43.870 --> 00:21:44.680
General...

00:21:45.220 --> 00:21:47.820
We must not attack first.

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.780
They've found us.

00:21:52.730 --> 00:21:54.070
Responding to Solomon.

00:21:54.070 --> 00:21:56.960
High likelihood of enemy materialization
within two hundred seconds.

00:21:56.960 --> 00:21:59.360
Route: 50. Speed down.

00:21:59.360 --> 00:22:01.020
Partial shield release.

00:22:01.020 --> 00:22:03.090
Kestrel, guide the transport craft for water landing.

00:22:03.090 --> 00:22:04.590
CDC to Grace.

00:22:04.920 --> 00:22:06.910
Initiate track as per regulations.

00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:07.590
Roger.

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.590
Remove reflective camouflage.

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:13.470
Inputting code.
Removing reflective camouflage!

00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:27.740
An island...

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:30.740
There really is an island!

00:22:31.450 --> 00:22:33.740
She really is here.

00:22:39.470 --> 00:22:41.590
Arrows, this is your graduation exam.

00:22:41.590 --> 00:22:43.180
I'm counting on you, little girl.

00:22:43.180 --> 00:22:44.060
Roger!

00:22:51.320 --> 00:22:55.110
In-flight C300, this is FA3. Code: Arrows.

00:22:55.110 --> 00:22:55.850
Please respond.

00:22:55.850 --> 00:22:57.800
Thank you for contacting us.

00:22:57.800 --> 00:23:01.050
This is C300. Code: Cetus.

00:23:01.050 --> 00:23:03.680
Human Army's South Asian Fleet,

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:07.150
Special Aerial Regiment, Perseus Company.

00:23:07.150 --> 00:23:10.110
Cetus, please follow my lead.

00:23:10.110 --> 00:23:13.650
Arrows, we will follow you completely. In return,

00:23:13.650 --> 00:23:15.870
please relay a message to your leader.

00:23:16.590 --> 00:23:20.870
Tell him our wish is to allow
our hope to meet your hope.

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:23.880
Hope?

00:23:54.660 --> 00:23:57.320
Through much sacrifice, we won peace.

00:23:58.470 --> 00:24:01.450
What did we want desperately enough to lose it?

00:24:03.200 --> 00:24:07.940
That day, an unknown hope visited us,
along with a new battle.

00:24:09.450 --> 00:24:12.910
It was the beginning of our end.

00:24:22.420 --> 00:24:25.510
<i>Fafner in the Azure: Exodus</i>, episode 2:

00:24:25.510 --> 00:24:26.980
The Name of Hope.
